        <body>
            <div xml:id="d230">

                <pb facs="0562" n="472" sameAs="frus:frus1875v01/pg472"/>

                <head>No. 226.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Washburne to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1875-08-03"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 3, 1875</date>.
                        (Received August 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1192.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In the National Assembly, on Thursday, the
                    29th ultimo, Mr. Raoul Duval, a Bonapartist deputy from the Seine Inferieure,
                    addressed an inquiry to the minister of foreign affairs in regard to what had
                    been done in the United States in relation to the claims of certain Frenchmen
                    who had suffered losses in our late war by the acts both of the army of the
                    Government and that of the rebels.</p>
                <p>I send herewith, for your information, a translation of the remarks of Mr. Raoul
                    Duval and of the answer made to him by the Duke Decazes.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>E. B. WASHBURNE.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d230-a1.xml" xpointer="d230-a1"/>
            </div>
